WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
good afternoon i'm assistant sheriff  andrew walsh i'm here to brief you today  on the additional details that we know  with regards to the officer-involved  shooting event that occurred on tuesday  september 21st 2021  this is officer-involved shooting number  six for 2021.  this is the third fatal officer-involved  shooting we've had so far this year  compared to the same time last year we  had 15 officer-involved shootings seven  of which were fatal  this event was called in as a battery  with a deadly weapon at 9 23 am on  september 21st 2021  the officer-involved shooting occurred  in the 300 block of south 11th street  las vegas nevada 89101  in the downtown area command and you can  see the image of this neighborhood on  the screen to my left  the involved officer is officer zachary  adam he is 41 years old and has been  with the las vegas metropolitan police  department since 2006. in this incident  officer adam was in was armed with a  larue tactical 308 rifle the  investigation revealed that officer adam  filed fired one round during this  incident  officer adam is assigned to the homeland  security division specifically as  assigned to the special weapons and  tactics bureau the swat team  the suspect in this incident was  identified as trent xavier leech he's he  was a 30 year old white male adult he  was five foot seven and weighed 200  pounds and mr leech's photograph is on  the screen to my left in this incident  mr leach was armed with a black  semi-automatic beretta apx nine  millimeter handgun and the investigation  revealed that he fired approximately 20  rounds during this incident  if he had survived mr leach would have  been charged with battery with a deadly  weapon assaulting a public officer with  a deadly weapon resisting a public  officer with a deadly weapon  discharging a firearm at or into an  occupied vehicle and discharging a  firearm from at or into an occupied  structure  the details of the officer involved  shooting are as follows on tuesday  september 21st 2021 at approximately 9  23 a.m the las vegas metropolitan police  department dispatch center received a  call from a citizen reporting that there  were two males in an argument and that  one of the males was armed with a  handgun  the address given by the caller was the  400 block of south 11th street  the male with the handgun was later  later identified as trent xavier leech  the two  las vegas metropolitan police officers  that were in the area investigating a  vacant property that needed to be  boarded up  responded to the area and found mr leach  and the other male  arguing in the alley near east 11th  street  the officers attempted to detain mr  leach but he refused and he fled on foot  and ran away from the officers as they  attempted to contact him  the officers initiated a flip suit and  followed mr leach until he made his way  into a vacant building located in the  300 block of south 11th street  the officers quickly recognized the need  to set up a perimeter on the building  and treat this situation as a barricaded  armed subject  our officers are trained to slow the  momentum and call in additional  resources in situations like this to  assist in de-escalating the situation  and attempting to communicate with the  suspect hopefully bringing incidents  like this to a peaceful resolution  shortly after swat and crisis  negotiators arrived a different male  that had been sleeping in the vacant  building came out and confirmed that mr  leech was inside the building and he was  armed with a handgun  our swat negotiation team attempted to  communicate with mr leach for several  hours and at some point during this  attempt to negotiate mr leach began  shooting from inside the building toward  the officers  through the cross of the barricade mr  leech fired approximately 20 rounds  and there were photos on the screen of  the bearcat from that swat utilizes  which you can see was struck by gunfire  and i believe there's a photograph of a  residence that's a second story window  of an apartment located directly to the  south of the building where mr leech was  that was occupied and struck by gunfire  during this incident  mr leach's reckless and dangerous  actions not only endangered the lives of  the officers but the lives of citizens  who live in the neighborhood at  approximately 2 33 p.m  while using the door frame of the church  that leads to the backyard  mr leech used the door frame as cover  and pointed his firearm towards the  officers  in response to mr leech pointing his  firearm at officers swat officer adam  fired one round from his rifle striking  mr leech  at this time a team of swat officers  then approached mr leech to provide  medical aid and medical personnel  pronounced him deceased at the scene  we'll now play some videos from this  incident the first video you're going to  see is from the actual initial contact  between the patrol officers from the  downtown area command and mr leach and  the original victim in this crime  hey come here  [Music]  that's the main guy with the fourth  gotcha  come here  give me your hand  get your hands out of your pocket  come on bro you're not even in trouble  here let's go  what are you gonna do  come here  let's go come here  you're just gonna make it worse bro come  on  talk to me  you're not in trouble  come on  just come here bro  so as you can see from that video that's  where the officers originally contacted  mr leach he ran from the original scene  and then was located in the alley just  about a block away  and you could see in that video where  the officers are attempting to  de-escalate the situation by shouting  commands at him and you could also hear  mr leech in that video yell shoot me now  this second video now is taken from  inside the structure where mr leach was  barricaded and we could play that from  here  so in this video you can see mr leech is  armed with a handgun and he comes into  the room where we had a robot  and he climbs on the robot and disables  the robot  and he has a close-up view of the  firearm  and in this last video this is moments  before the officer filed the ram fired  the round and you'll see the firearm  come out from behind the door pointed in  the direction of the swat officers and  the officers that had set up containment  on the building  and as i said earlier this occurs at the  end of mr leech firing approximately 20  rounds from inside of the structure  and that's the same video that's the  same prior to the shot being fired you  can see mr leech standing in the doorway  this is taken from one of our robots  that was deployed and you can see him  reaching out from beyond the door jamb  and pointing his firearm at the officers  and that concludes our briefing  we did have drones and robots deployed  but in this instance what the footage  you see here is from the robots  yes and you can get that from our  records bureau that's available upon  your request how close were the officers  when he's pointing his gun out  i think we came up with 40 feet was the  measurement of where the sniper was  where's the 170 yards 107 yards  207 feet  we can ask for the specifics  uh i'm not going to discuss the criminal  history it's just something that in  these briefings where in the past we  discussed criminal history and we're  vilified for talking about someone's  criminal history so that's available  upon you can go to our records bureau  and through the normal channels because  we  we're just not going to do that  right no we had no civilians injured  luckily in this incident uh only  the first civilian that mr leech had the  encounter with he was struck in the face  with firearm by mr leach so that is  where one of the counts of  would have would have applied  to him it was we had a civilian victim  but not from the structure  not from the firing inside the structure  those residences as close to they  weren't as how many rounds were being  fired were very  pro it's problematic for us to attempt  to  evacuate those so folks were sheltering  in place  and you could see how close they were  any charges for the other  person involved in that  fight or any idea no he was a victim  all right  thank you all very much

